&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our Internship&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Kick-start your career in finance with the Schonfeld Summer Internship! Over the course of 10 action-packed weeks, you will have the opportunity to build solutions that tackle real-world challenges and leave a lasting impact on the firm. As an intern, you’ll join a close-knit team that is ready to support your growth and accelerate your career. We will pair you with a dedicated manager and a mentor who’ll guide your development over the course of the internship and beyond. Throughout the program, you will have the chance to connect with senior leaders through a series of learning sessions, attend hands-on skills workshops, network at social events and get a behind-the-scenes look at how various functions power the firm. We’ll empower you to bring your ideas to life and make an impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Who We Are &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our Culture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;__symantecMPKIClientDetector&quot; style=&quot;display: none;&quot;&gt;__PRESENT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT EXODUSPOINT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ExodusPoint Capital&lt;/strong&gt;, founded in 2017 by Michael Gelband, began managing investor capital in 2018. The firm employs a global multi-strategy investment approach, seeking to deliver compelling asymmetric returns by combining complementary liquid strategies managed by experienced investment professionals within a robust risk framework. ExodusPoint brings together an accomplished team with hands-on experience running multi-manager businesses to create an institutional investment management firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ExodusPoint is looking for a Quantitative Intern to join a Corporate Credit investment team in Philadelphia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with the team’s traders, helping build the analytics and tools they use to monitor markets, identify opportunities and manage risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team trades investment-grade Corporate Credit across new issues and secondary markets. The role will be particularly focused on the quantitative side of the investment process – working with market and trading data, developing analytics, automating existing processes and finding better ways to present information to the desk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t require previous Credit or finance experience. We are looking for someone who is highly analytical, comfortable coding and interested in applying those skills to a live trading environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and analytics for the trading team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse market, pricing and trading data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop tools to identify relative-value opportunities and market dislocations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve intraday P&amp;amp;L, position and risk analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse liquidity and dealer activity across Corporate Credit markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate existing data and analytical processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve data pipelines used by the desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backtest quantitative ideas and help assess whether they are useful in practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with traders to understand problems and build practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use tools such as Claude Code and Codex to improve the speed and efficiency of development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work will be driven by problems the team is dealing with day-to-day. We want someone who is comfortable taking an idea or loosely defined problem and figuring out how to solve it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently studying, or recently completed, a degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Physics, Engineering, Data Science or another quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills, particularly Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with data and quantitative analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A good understanding of statistics and probability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using modern coding and AI development tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, self-motivated and comfortable working independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An interest in markets and trading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A combination of Computer Science and Mathematics / Statistics would be particularly relevant, although we are open to candidates from a range of quantitative backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graduate-level study is helpful but not required.,You do not need to have worked in Credit or financial markets before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care more about whether you can code, work with data and think through quantitative problems. Previous experience or coursework in markets, quantitative finance, machine learning or trading is useful, but not essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will sit directly with the investment team in Philadelphia and see how the tools you build are used in the trading process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is intended to be an in-person, full-time internship lasting approximately 3–4 months. Candidates do not need to currently live or study in Philadelphia, but should be able to work from the Philadelphia office during the internship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There may be scope for a longer-term opportunity depending on performance and the needs of the team.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;About Marshall Wace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Marshall Wace is a leading provider of alternative investment solutions with over $90 billion in assets under management. Our global investment process operates around the clock, deploying capital across a diverse range of systematic and fundamental strategies. We have a track record of providing market leading returns for over 25 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our success is underpinned by a perpetual effort to innovate and optimize upon our existing investment process, embracing sophisticated, proprietary technology and data sources at every level of the organization. Our small, but impactful group fosters a collegial culture that demands entrepreneurship and personal responsibility, presenting ample opportunity to employees for meaningful impact on our profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Intern Program&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 10 week Summer Intern Program includes the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business critical projects and problems to solve, with the opportunity to produce high-impact work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly personalized mentoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly lunch seminars with senior managers across all teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to participate in charitable events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance days hosted by other financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations Internship – Summer 2027&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a self‑motivated undergraduate senior student who is passionate about learning, problem solving, and efficiency in the context of global financial markets. Based in New York, you will join our Global Operations team and contribute to a high‑volume, technology‑driven investment management environment. Interns gain a front‑row view of how operational excellence and automation underpin the success of a leading hedge fund, while delivering real value through both tactical work and dedicated projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a close‑knit, technical operations team to support the firm’s activity across multiple markets and asset classes, including equities, credit, volatility, macro, and fixed income.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build knowledge of core operational processes such as trade processing, securities lending, settlement, asset servicing, data management, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an understanding of how automation, data analytics, and AI‑driven solutions enable the firm to manage a high volume of global trading efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Python, SQL, and other programming tools to analyze and manipulate data, and contribute to automation and AI initiatives that enhance operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify workflow and system improvements and partner with the team to implement change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with colleagues across Trading, Investment Analysis, Risk, Treasury, and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend seminars hosted by prime brokerage counterparties to learn how the buy side and sell side interact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates graduating between December 2027 and June 2028.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working toward a bachelor’s degree in a related field such as (but not limited to) Finance, Economics, Computer Science, Mathematics, or Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum cumulative GPA of 3.5.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills (verbal and written) and strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage time effectively and proactively engage with team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated curiosity about financial markets and enthusiasm for data‑driven and AI‑enabled process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div data-block=&quot;true&quot; data-editor=&quot;7ptjg&quot; data-offset-key=&quot;cspbn-0-0&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;public-DraftStyleDefault-block public-DraftStyleDefault-ltr&quot; data-offset-key=&quot;cspbn-0-0&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AQR Capital Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AQR is a global investment firm built at the intersection of financial theory and practical application. We strive to deliver concrete, long-term results by looking past market noise to identify and isolate the factors that matter most, and by developing ideas that stand up to rigorous testing. By putting theory into practice, we have become a leader in alternative strategies and an innovator in traditional portfolio management since 1998.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At AQR, our employees share a common spirit of academic excellence, intellectual honesty, and an unwavering commitment to seeking the truth. We’re determined to know what makes financial markets tick – and we’ll ask every question and challenge every assumption. &amp;nbsp;We recognize and respect the power of collaboration and believe transparency and openness to new ideas leads to innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Internship Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 10-week summer program puts real work of the firm in your hands. You will work alongside brilliant people, gain insights and know-how from our Quanta Academy Summer Term&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; curriculum, and experience what it’s like to work at the pinnacle of global, systematic investing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learning is the cornerstone of our culture and plays an active role in the internship experience — through daily collaboration and interaction with employees at all levels, in workshops and classes, and most significantly by working on projects that matter to the many clients we serve. Our unique AQR Quanta Academy: Summer Term learning series, a structured program, consists of over 40 hours of educational, skill-building and networking events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AQR is looking for exceptionally talented students to join our team as Summer Analysts within the Business Development group. Interns will be placed on one of two teams within the department:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;U.S. Institutional&lt;/strong&gt;, whose objective is to identify and develop relationships with prospective investors and strengthen relationships with existing clients and investment consultants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;U.S. Wealth&lt;/strong&gt;, who engages with taxable U.S. investors and their advisors. The team is responsible for education, awareness and managing new and current client relationships for AQR strategies through dedicated coverage to the Family Office community, Registered Investment Advisor community, as well as elite advisors and teams within the major Broker-Dealer segment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will work alongside senior members of the teams to build upon AQR’s presence, with a focus on developing new and maintaining existing relationships with clients in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn to interact with the world’s most sophisticated investors and senior investment management professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a comprehensive technical knowledge of AQR’s full suite of products, the functions and responsibilities of key employees, and the competitive landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support senior team members as they determine business strategy including new product development and new business lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get active exposure to senior leadership of AQR’s investment teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with other members of Business Development to leverage the firm’s intellectual capital and customize marketing materials for prospects and existing clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marshall the full resources of the firm to coordinate responses to investor inquiries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;December 2027 or Spring 2028 graduate in Economics, Finance, Business or a Science, Quantitative, or Engineering Program from a top university is preferred. Liberal arts students with appropriate work experience will also be considered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hard working and eager to learn in a highly intellectual, collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-organized and detail-oriented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic about developing and implementing ideas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical and problem- solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presents and communicates with maturity, credibility, and clarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly proficient in PowerPoint and Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;AQR is an Equal Opportunity Employer.&amp;nbsp; EEO/VET/DISABILITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AQR Capital Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AQR is a global investment firm built at the intersection of financial theory and practical application. We strive to deliver concrete, long-term results by looking past market noise to identify and isolate the factors that matter most, and by developing ideas that stand up to rigorous testing. By putting theory into practice, we have become a leader in alternative strategies and an innovator in traditional portfolio management since 1998.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At AQR, our employees share a common spirit of academic excellence, intellectual honesty and an unwavering commitment to seeking the truth. We’re determined to know what makes financial markets tick – and we’ll ask every question and challenge every assumption. &amp;nbsp;We recognize and respect the power of collaboration and believe transparency and openness to new ideas leads to innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Internship Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 10-week summer program puts real work of the firm in your hands. You will work alongside brilliant people, gain insights and know-how from our Quanta Academy Summer Term&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; curriculum, and experience what it’s like to work at the pinnacle of global, systematic investing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learning is the cornerstone of our culture and plays an active role in the internship experience — through daily collaboration and interaction with employees at all levels, in workshops and classes, and most significantly by working on projects that matter to the&amp;nbsp;many clients&amp;nbsp;we serve.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Our unique AQR Quanta Academy: Summer Term learning series, a structured program, consists of over 40 hours of educational, skill-building and networking events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you an intelligent and creative thinker? &amp;nbsp;Do you enjoy finding elegant technical solutions to complex problems? Are you interested in seeing an impact of your work in real life? We are looking for innovative and passionate undergraduates to join our engineering teams as summer analysts.&amp;nbsp; Candidates may be interviewed for one of several teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Summer Analyst, you will work on meaningful projects that support a wide range of business and investment functions across the firm. You will collaborate closely with engineers, researchers, and business stakeholders to design, develop, test, and deploy solutions in a fast-paced, highly collaborative environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Projects may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building scalable applications and services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing user interfaces and data visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing APIs and backend systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with large and complex datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhancing cloud-based infrastructure and distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving developer tools, automation, and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Researching and implementing innovative technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will gain exposure to modern software engineering practices and technologies while contributing to systems that are critical to the firm’s operations and investment processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our engineering teams work with a broad range of technologies, which may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python, Java, C#, Go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web technologies and modern frontend frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud platforms and distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databases, messaging systems, and data platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visualization and analytics tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Version control, CI/CD, and automation frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who You Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finishing either a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree program between December 2027 and June 2028&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mature and thoughtful, with the ability to operate within a collaborative, team-oriented culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hard working and eager to learn in a highly intellectual, innovative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look beyond the surface level to understand the underlying details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AQR is an Equal Opportunity Employer.&amp;nbsp; EEO/VET/DISABILITY&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MKTQ427R39&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks is hiring a Director of International Communications to build and scale our global communications strategy. As Databricks grows its footprint, this role will own how that story gets told: new market entries, in-country investments, new offices, customer wins, and local business milestones that build Databricks&#39; reputation market by market. This role will serve as a strategic communications advisor to regional and country leaders in Europe, Asia, and the Americas and will be responsible for the execution of communications programs across those regions. This is a strategic role: turning business momentum into locally resonant news that establishes Databricks as a leader in data and AI around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What This Role Unlocks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communications advisor to regional leaders – &lt;/strong&gt;advise on PR, social, internal comms strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional news at scale&lt;/strong&gt; — a dedicated strategy for translating business growth across Europe, Asia, and the Americas into press moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local relevance, global consistency&lt;/strong&gt; — an approach tailored to each region&#39;s media landscape while staying true to Databricks&#39; global product and corporate narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong in-market presence&lt;/strong&gt; — deep relationships with regional leadership, agencies, and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership for regional PR teams&lt;/strong&gt; — a dedicated manager and mentor for our international communications leads while building close relationships with U.S. based comms and product leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Communications Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Databricks&#39; international communications strategy across three regions: Europe, Asia, and the Americas (13 countries).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot and drive market-specific news — expansions, investments, new offices, customer milestones, and partnerships — that builds Databricks&#39; profile in each country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the communications strategy as the business scales into new and existing regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the connective tissue between global communications strategy and on-the-ground business momentum in every region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional business leaders, ensuring strategy reflects local business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with field marketing and country managers to identify stories worth telling on the ground&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Agency/Media Relationships&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and support Databricks&#39; communications leads internationally; set clear direction and priorities while providing the autonomy to run their markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage PR agency relationships across all 13 covered markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build direct relationships with key regional media so each market has the storytelling support it needs to land Databricks&#39; news locally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in international, regional, or global communications, ideally in enterprise software, cloud, or AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record building regional press strategies and driving coverage across multiple international markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong people management experience, with a track record of developing communications professionals across international teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing PR agencies across diverse regions and media landscapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building skills with senior business leaders and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharp news judgment — able to spot and shape a story from business developments like market entries, customer wins, or new offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating across time zones and cultures, balancing global consistency with local relevance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel internationally as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As an Applied Science Intern, you will join a cross-functional team of engineers and applied scientists building AI-powered features within the Datadog platform. You will contribute to both existing and new products by improving machine learning models, developing new AI capabilities, and helping bring research into production. Working closely with engineering and product partners, you&#39;ll gain hands-on experience deploying AI systems at scale while strengthening your product mindset, collaboration, and communication skills. You&#39;ll also have opportunities to contribute to cutting-edge research that directly powers customer-facing features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design solutions for AI use cases by researching and benchmarking state-of-the-art models to identify the best approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build highly scalable product features using generative AI, machine learning algorithms, and statistical techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the development, deployment, monitoring, and maintenance of production AI models, services, and infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore, analyze, and derive insights from the large-scale observability data flowing through Datadog systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in technical knowledge sharing by presenting recent academic research and investigating emerging model architectures to improve existing and future products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering and product teams to productionize AI solutions and deliver customer-facing features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will graduate in&lt;strong&gt; 2027 &lt;/strong&gt;with a degree in Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Statistics, Computer Science, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building machine learning models through coursework, research, internships, or personal projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong programming skills and are eager to learn new languages and technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate complex technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong interest in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and data-driven product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to complete a 6-month internship beginning in&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;February, March, April, May, or June 2027 (we are unable to accommodate internships starting at any other time)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We know not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That’s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your experience, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on meaningful technical challenges alongside engineers across the globe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in mentorship and buddy programs designed to support learning and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join an in-person intern cohort, attend company social events, and engage with Datadog Community Guilds and employee resource groups throughout the internship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive relocation support and travel benefits where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy office perks including snacks, drinks, and catered lunches on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please ensure that you submit your CV/resume in English. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If possible, please apply using your personal email address instead of your university email address.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Students can sign up for a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/datadog-github-student-developer-pack/&quot;&gt;free Datadog Pro account&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our platform and products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Datadog:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is the leading observability and security platform for the AI era, providing businesses with unified visibility across the technology stack to manage complexity at scale. It brings applications, infrastructure, data, models, and security into one place, using AI to detect and resolve issues before they impact customers. Trusted globally by Fortune 500 companies and high-growth AI leaders, Datadog enables businesses to move faster with clarity and confidence. Learn more about #DatadogLife on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/datadoghq/?hl=en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/datadog&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;LinkedIn,&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://learn.datadoghq.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Datadog Learning Center. &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;215&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity at Datadog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog is proud to offer &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;equal employment opportunity&lt;/a&gt; to everyone regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, veteran status, and other characteristics protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements. Here are our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/candidate-legal-notices/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Legal Notices&lt;/a&gt; for your reference.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Datadog endeavors to make our Careers Page accessible to all users. If you would like to contact us regarding the accessibility of our website or need assistance completing the application process, please complete &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeoJeduEZ2NdZF_65uZmWUrCM-zee7yADXX1s6Xr9zAGq8iKA/viewform&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt;. This form is for accommodation requests only and cannot be used to inquire about the status of applications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Privacy and AI Guidelines:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Available Locations:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Lisbon, Portugal&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Department&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Emerging Technologies &amp;amp; Incubation (ETI) is where new and bold products are built and released within Cloudflare. Rather than being constrained by the structures which make Cloudflare a hugely successful business, we are able to leverage them to deliver entirely new tools and products to our customers. Cloudflare’s edge and network make it possible to solve problems at massive scale and efficiency which would be impossible for almost any other organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build products at the intersection of AI, search and retrieval, data insights, and product engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As AI agents change how people discover and interact with the Internet, new problems are emerging around how content is found, understood, retrieved, and kept current. Cloudflare is uniquely positioned to help website owners make their content discoverable and to help agents find relevant, trustworthy information across our network. Building these capabilities requires solving problems across distributed systems, crawling, content ingestion, indexing, retrieval quality, developer experience, and reliable product delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare also has a unique perspective on how the Internet is changing. Our global network observes signals that can help us understand trends, identify when content changes, and measure the pulse of the Internet. Used responsibly, these signals could improve existing products, help customers and AI companies find fresher and more relevant information, and create entirely new capabilities and products.&amp;nbsp;The opportunity is broad and still evolving. We need to deliver excellent products today while continuing to identify the problems Cloudflare is uniquely positioned to solve next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a tight-knit group that communicates and collaborates regularly. We celebrate our achievements, support each other when we make mistakes, and hold each other and our work to a high standard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Engineering Manager to lead engineering across some of our AI and Internet Data Insights portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for the people, execution, and engineering quality behind products that help customers make their content discoverable and turn complex Internet signals into useful experiences. You will partner closely with Product Management and engineering teams across Cloudflare to deliver current priorities and shape future opportunities.&amp;nbsp;This is a management role for someone who is deeply technically credible. You will not be expected to write most of the code, but you should be able to understand the systems your engineers operate, challenge architectural decisions, ask the right questions when something is going wrong, and step into a technical problem when the situation calls for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the same time, we are looking for a manager, not a tech lead with direct reports. Your success will be measured by the quality and output of the team you build, the engineers you develop, and the systems and products they deliver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may require flexibility to be on-call outside of standard working hours to address technical issues as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, coach, and grow engineers working across AI-powered search, Internet data insights, and customer-facing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own execution by establishing clear priorities, creating predictable delivery, and giving engineers the context and autonomy to own meaningful areas of the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of search and retrieval capabilities that help people and AI agents find relevant, trustworthy, and current content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Management to understand customer problems, shape the roadmap, and turn broad opportunities into clear engineering outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help identify how signals from Cloudflare&#39;s global network can produce useful and trustworthy insights for customers, partners, and other Cloudflare products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore where Cloudflare&#39;s unique view of Internet activity can improve content discovery, enable new product experiences, or support entirely new products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance near-term product delivery with thoughtful technical investments that allow promising ideas to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational health of the systems in your area, including observability, incident response, data and search quality, and long-term reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop technical leaders and create space for engineers to lead architecture and implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want you to love it here. This role is a great fit for you if:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led and developed high-performing engineering team(s) and can point to what that team shipped and how the people on it grew.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are technically credible with experienced engineers. You can review a design, understand the trade-offs in a distributed system or data platform, and recognize when a technical problem needs deeper investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable managing a team working across several related technical areas and can create clarity without requiring every problem to fit neatly into a single box.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care deeply about reliability and quality, particularly when the output of a system is data that people use to understand the Internet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong product judgment and enjoy working with Product Management to decide what is worth building, what needs improvement and what should not be built at all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with ambiguity and with finding structure in areas where the opportunity is clearer than the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly, give direct feedback, and can explain complex technical decisions to both engineers and non-engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Examples of Desirable Skills, Knowledge, and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical grounding in distributed systems, search systems, data-intensive systems, Internet infrastructure, or adjacent areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating products involving crawling, content ingestion, indexing, retrieval, analytics, or large-scale data processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating systems where correctness, reliability, and quality matter as much as feature delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hiring, developing, and retaining strong engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Product Management to shape and execute a roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking products or major capabilities from an ambiguous opportunity to a clear customer outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), which combines information retrieval with generative AI to produce answers grounded in selected source material.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products for AI developers, AI agents, publishers, or content-heavy websites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large-scale telemetry or Internet-scale datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning complex underlying systems or data into useful products for a broad audience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Cloudflare Radar, Internet measurement research, or the broader ecosystem of tools used to understand Internet performance, availability and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For Portugal based hires: Estimated annual salary of €74,000 - €&lt;span class=&quot;cell-value&quot;&gt;111,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;cell-value&quot;&gt;The final offer will be inclusive of time exemption, in alignment with the applicable law and collective bargaining agreements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is eligible to participate in Cloudflare’s equity plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;What Makes Cloudflare Special?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re not just a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company. We’re a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company with a soul. Fundamental to our mission to help build a better Internet is protecting the free and open Internet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/protecting-free-expression-online/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Galileo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: Since 2014, we&#39;ve equipped more than 2,400 journalism and civil society organizations in 111 countries with powerful tools to defend themselves against attacks that would otherwise censor their work, technology already used by Cloudflare’s enterprise customers--at no cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/athenian/&quot;&gt;Athenian Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: In 2017, we created the Athenian Project to ensure that state and local governments have the highest level of protection and reliability for free, so that their constituents have access to election information and voter registration. Since the project, we&#39;ve provided services to more than 425 local government election websites in 33 states.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: We released&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to help fix the foundation of the Internet by building a faster, more secure and privacy-centric public DNS resolver. This is available publicly for everyone to use - it is the first consumer-focused service Cloudflare has ever released. Here’s the deal - we don’t store client IP addresses never, ever. We will continue to abide by our&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/1.1.1.1/privacy/public-dns-resolver&quot;&gt; privacy commitment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and ensure that no user data is sold to advertisers or used to target consumers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Sound like something you’d like to be a part of? We’d love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that applicants who progress to the offer stage of the interview process may be asked to attend an in-person interview within one of the Cloudflare Offices or Cloudflare Hubs.&amp;nbsp; More details about this will be available at that stage of the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position may require access to information protected under U.S. export control laws, including the U.S. Export Administration Regulations. Please note that any offer of employment may be conditioned on your authorization to receive software or technology controlled under these U.S. export laws without sponsorship for an export license.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people and place great value in both diversity and inclusiveness. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to their, or any other person&#39;s, perceived or actual&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, family care status, or any other basis protected by law. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an AA/Veterans/Disabled Employer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. &amp;nbsp;Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job. Examples of reasonable accommodations include, but are not limited to, changing the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. &amp;nbsp;If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job, please contact us via e-mail at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;hr@cloudflare.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; or via mail at 101 Townsend St. San Francisco, CA 94107.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are excited to offer an opportunity for a diverse group of talented students to join the internship program at Schonfeld. You’ll spend ten weeks within our Core Operations team where you will work directly with Operations senior management and across peer groups in all areas, while being immersed in the culture and atmosphere of Schonfeld, working alongside talented professionals on high profile projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Operations team at Schonfeld take on a wide range of responsibilities and challenges. They are responsible for the trade life cycle and that includes everything from supporting trading and portfolio managers all the way through to trade settlement. In operations you will collaborate with many peers from different departments, such as but not limited to Risk, Portfolio Financing and Fund Accounting. Operations touches upon many different facets as we are responsible for ensuring the investment side of the business can deploy their investment strategies. The Operations team is best in class in supporting policies and procedures for optimal efficiency.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;18&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Body Text&quot;&gt;Help to implement best in class reconciliation across cash, positions, and trades&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;469777462&amp;quot;:[9630],&amp;quot;469777927&amp;quot;:[0],&amp;quot;469777928&amp;quot;:[1]}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
